    <statement>For positive integer k>1, let f(k) be the number of ways of factoring k into product of positive integers greater than 1 (order of factors not counted). Prove: If n is a positive integer greater than 1, p is a prime factor of n, then f(n) ≤ n/p.</statement>
    <domain>number_theory</domain>
